ver, because the effect is extreme relative to the outcome scale, was prompted by an initially rejected opposite-direction screen, and could reflect coding, distributional, or subgroup-coding artifacts, I do not accept H131/H132 or H120 yet. I request independent validation of the overall H120 claim to test whether this unusually large association replicates outside the discovery sample before accepting the feature_027 conclusion. If validation is positive and threshold-aligned, I will reconsider accepting H120 and the subgroup claims; if it is null, opposite, or overly unstable, I will close the family as a dataset-specific anomaly. All statements remain associations in this dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
