  "narrative": "The new subgroup analyses strongly confirm the already validated outcome_014 feature_027=1 versus 0 association. For the registered +1 direction, H133-H136, H138-H140 all have signed mean differences of about +0.79 to +0.81 with 95% intervals entirely above zero and far above the outcome_014 10% absolute-mean benchmark of about 0.0093; cell sizes are adequate. I accept these as dataset-specific subgroup associations. The earlier feature_034 subgroup claims H131 and H132 have similarly enormous direct discovery estimates, so I also accept them as dataset-specific subgroup associations. These subgroup conclusions do not change the scientific interpretation: the main finding remains an exceptionally large measured association in this supplied dataset, not a causal or generalizable biological effect. The feature_002 interaction H137 is centered near zero, which supports stability of the main contrast rather than positive effect modification, but it does not support the registered positive interaction claim, so I reject it. H141 has a positive point estimate above the threshold, but the interval includes zero and lower values below the threshold; I reject the positive interaction claim as unsupported, while acknowledging this is not proof that no small modification exists. H142 is near zero/negative and imprecise; it is also rejected as a positive interaction claim. The feature_023 stratified tests are not convincing: H143 has a positive point near the threshold but very wide uncertainty and only 40 exposed observations; H144 is positive but not threshold-robust, with an interval spanning opposite effects. Their overall parent H119 had a larger unadjusted estimate but an interval spanning zero, and the stratified attenuation is consistent with confounding or imbalance involving the very large feature_027 contrast rather than an independent feature_023 effect. Combined with the incoherent cross-outcome feature_023 screen and the wide, non-robust validation of H118, I reject H118, H119, H143, and H144 as unsupported feature_023 associations in this dataset. Reject means the directional claims are not supported by the accumulated evidence, not that every possible small effect has been proved absent. No validation is requested because the main feature_027 association is already independently validated, the new subgroup confirmations are internally consistent and extremely large, and additional validation of low-prior or imprecise feature_023/interaction hypotheses has low marginal scientific value.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 11 appraise. Accepted conclusions now include H120 overall and the outcome_014 feature_027 subgroup mean-difference claims H131-H136, H138-H140. All are dataset-specific measured associations; direction +1 means feature_027=1 is associated with much weaker dependency, i.e. a less negative outcome_014 score. Effect magnitudes are about 85 times the outcome_014 10% absolute-mean benchmark, and the pattern is stable across feature_034, feature_002, feature_060, feature_055 level_003/level_001, and log-PFS median split. Positive interaction claims H137, H141, and H142 are rejected/closed: no robust positive effect modification, although intervals do not fully exclude modest modification. The feature_023 family is closed: H118, H119, H143, and H144 are rejected/closed. The feature_023 overall signal appears imprecise, low-prior, cross-outcome incoherent, and plausibly confounded by feature_027 imbalance. No validation requested. Future priorities: avoid redundant feature_027 subgroup checks and low-prior feature_023 follow-up; use remaining cycles on untested predictors with adequate cell counts, while continuing to distinguish measured associations from causal or generalizable claims."
}

