  "narrative": "No assessments are currently due, but two outcome-specific feature_027 claims now have direct discovery evidence and can be settled. H153 asks whether outcome_011 is weaker for feature_027=1 versus 0; its signed estimate is -0.007 with a 95% interval from -0.037 to 0.023. For outcome_011, the approximate 10% absolute-mean benchmark is around 0.030, so the interval is compatible with null and opposite effects and does not even credibly reach the positive-threshold region. I therefore reject and close H153 as a positive association in this dataset. H156 asks the analogous positive-direction question for outcome_015; its signed estimate is -0.0177 with interval -0.0369 to 0.0016. Although the absolute point is somewhat large, it is in the opposite direction from the registered positive hypothesis and the interval crosses null with an upper bound well below the positive-threshold region. I reject and close H156 for the weaker-dependency direction; this does not settle the separate opposite-direction outcome_015 question represented by H61.\n\nThe most useful next allocation is to complete the outcome-specificity screen for the accepted feature_027 marker. The accepted finding is not that feature_027 has broad biological relevance; rather, H120 and related subgroup claims support a very large association specifically with outcome_014. The remaining active untested feature_027 claims cover outcome_001, outcome_002, outcome_003, outcome_004, outcome_005, outcome_007, outcome_009, outcome_010, outcome_012, outcome_013, and outcome_016 with the registered positive direction. Null or modest results there would strengthen the conclusion that the feature_027 association is outcome-specific in this supplied dataset. A threshold-aligned large positive result would be genuinely informative and would justify focused validation.\n\nI also register one targeted refinement of the accepted H120 contrast: outcome_014 feature_027=1 versus 0 within the feature_023=0 subgroup. This is complementary to H143/H144, which tested the feature_023 contrast within feature_027 strata. Because feature_023 was the only other feature with a comparatively large outcome_014 signal but was not robust, an important alternative is that the feature_027 contrast is aliased with feature_023 status. If the feature_027 association is broadly stable, I expect a large positive mean difference within feature_023=0, roughly in the same direction and order of magnitude as the overall H120 contrast. If the association is absent, very attenuated, or reversed in feature_023=0, the accepted H120 finding would be better described as concentrated in, or plausibly confounded by, feature_023 coding patterns in this dataset rather than as a broad dataset-specific marker of outcome_014 dependency. The cell sizes are adequate: approximately 40 exposed feature_027=1 subjects within feature_023=0 and 195 comparator subjects, plus large complement cells. This remains an association analysis only and should not be interpreted causally or as generalizable.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 explore. Rejected/closed H153 (outcome_011 feature_027 weaker-dependency claim) and H156 (outcome_015 feature_027 weaker-dependency claim) because signed intervals were null-centering/wrong direction and not threshold-supported. H61 remains the separate opposite-direction outcome_015/feature_027 question and was not reassessed. Accepted main result remains H120: outcome_014 feature_027=1 versus 0 is associated with dramatically weaker dependency in this dataset, replicated and robust across many tested strata; no supported positive effect modification by feature_002, feature_055 level_003, or feature_024 median split. Next priority is the outcome-specificity screen for feature_027 across remaining outcomes: H145-H152, H154, H155, and H157. One new refinement is registered: outcome_014 feature_027=1 versus 0 within feature_023=0. This tests whether the huge feature_027 signal is robust to the main unresolved secondary feature_023 signal or appears feature_023-aliased. Preserve validation budget for a genuinely threshold-aligned new feature_027 outcome association or for resolving a decisive feature_023 stratification result. All conclusions are measured associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable claims."
